        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "27267d4f-0378-3b52-8142-616383f4a35f",
                "word": "collégialité",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "95cc89e7-6eb7-4da9-bbbb-5664782e007f",
                        "entry_id": "27267d4f-0378-3b52-8142-616383f4a35f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "collégialités"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d5ec816d-09fe-3138-9bc3-af69a5b3e550",
                        "entry_id": "27267d4f-0378-3b52-8142-616383f4a35f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Caractère de ce qui est collégial."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b934ce2c-7c2e-43a2-adca-f82e8be1d39e",
                                "sense_id": "d5ec816d-09fe-3138-9bc3-af69a5b3e550",
                                "text": "Collégialité d’une direction."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "58fd579f-cff8-45a8-b5b8-b020b7f8ef33",
                                "sense_id": "d5ec816d-09fe-3138-9bc3-af69a5b3e550",
                                "text": "La collégialité n’est cependant pas uniquement une règle de procédure."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8acce04-5008-4b49-a639-a2c828dfa150",
                                "sense_id": "d5ec816d-09fe-3138-9bc3-af69a5b3e550",
                                "text": "Elle indique également la méthode : la “collégialité”. Chaque personne ne peut à elle seule avoir les compétences de comptable, de juriste, de géomètre, etc. La collégialité est une réponse à la complexité et au manque de personnel."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "14747f19-6568-39c9-baa1-2523edfb91df",
                        "entry_id": "27267d4f-0378-3b52-8142-616383f4a35f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Coopération réciproque entre les membres d'une communauté qui agissent comme des collègues."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "69a65979-c31a-48ac-afbc-0b76ae7e882b",
                                "sense_id": "14747f19-6568-39c9-baa1-2523edfb91df",
                                "text": "La collégialité que nous associons au soutien réciproque informel devient synonyme de convivialité dans un climat d’acceptation, de respect, de confiance nécessaire à l’engagement dans la coopération"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9705911a-7cdb-489b-b9c5-787e4cc774b7",
                        "source_entry_id": "27267d4f-0378-3b52-8142-616383f4a35f",
                        "target_lang_word": "collegiality",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "collegiality",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3d825f1d-96cc-3ba3-bad0-3073159abb6b",
                                        "entry_id": "9dd51617-2953-3d43-bdf3-f38058d616a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "collegial atmosphere; working with colleagues in an effective and cooperative manner"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd6130a8-41f1-466e-b9cd-60e5887ca80e",
                                                "sense_id": "3d825f1d-96cc-3ba3-bad0-3073159abb6b",
                                                "text": "To what extent does collegiality still exist in the management here?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db0d44a1-3b0f-46d5-a136-b21d507c4343",
                                                "sense_id": "3d825f1d-96cc-3ba3-bad0-3073159abb6b",
                                                "text": "Within a global law firm there is plainly a need for a common culture and collegiality: every lawyer a client deals with anywhere in the world is a representative of the firm and needs to exhibit common values. The teamwork which is critical to a global firm strategy is based on a collegial approach."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed7f7410-09f1-47e6-9004-c1218a3f5781",
                                                "sense_id": "3d825f1d-96cc-3ba3-bad0-3073159abb6b",
                                                "text": "Second, most of the justices suggested that informal norms of collegiality and respect for the opinions of colleagues often resulted in deliberate efforts to find acceptable compromise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af15f8f8-e797-3b36-a236-1a3176960042",
                                        "entry_id": "9dd51617-2953-3d43-bdf3-f38058d616a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "power and authority that is shared among peers, especially the sharing of collegiate power among Roman Catholic bishops."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d3f7467-5aef-4f75-80c8-4a224d4781ac",
                                                "sense_id": "af15f8f8-e797-3b36-a236-1a3176960042",
                                                "text": "But collegiality does refer to a kind of sharing of authority between Rome and all the other local churches. Each bishop represents his own local church, and the pope represents the local church of Rome which, by tradition, exercises a primacy of love over all the other local churches and has become the church-of-last-resort in disputed questions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb293477-9b29-4394-a596-a90862b5837b",
                                                "sense_id": "af15f8f8-e797-3b36-a236-1a3176960042",
                                                "text": "For all the criticisms of John Paul's practice of collegiality, there is no doubt that he spoke often and highly of its importance. From his very first Urbi et Orbi address, given the day after his election, where he spoke of the “special bond, that is, collegiality” which “binds together the sacred pastors” [..] the collegiality of the bishops was a thread running through his pontificate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "feb7f4d5-5075-4592-9210-502bcd8d3bcf",
